{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isUnbroken","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV10isUnbrokenSbSgvp","role":"symbol","title":"isUnbroken","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isUnbroken","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"unbroken","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/isunbroken"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/isUnbroken","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/isUnbroken":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isUnbroken","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/isunbroken","type":"topic","title":"isUnbroken","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/isUnbroken","kind":"symbol"}}}